=== start ===
Felix: I've prepared a padded stand for the watch. The original chain can rest beside it without putting strain on the links.
Keiko: That's wonderful! The children will be delighted.
Andy: And the sheriff will be delighted not to investigate another disappearance.
Farmer: You seem relieved.
Andy: I've spent all this time worrying about a watch that was exactly where someone intended it to be.
Felix: An understandable oversight, Sheriff.
Andy: Thank you, Felix.
+ [Let the children introduce the repaired watch.]
    Farmer: Why not let the children introduce it? They've done all the research.
    Keiko: That's a lovely idea.
    Andy: Then I believe our youngest historians should have the honor.
    The children proudly explain the watch's history. When Keiko opens the display, the watch ticks steadily.
    Keiko: Listen! It's working again.
    Andy: Best sound I've heard all week.
    -> closing
+ [Encourage Keiko to tell everyone about the surprise.]
    Farmer: Keiko, perhaps you could explain why you wanted the watch repaired.
    Keiko: I'd be happy to.
    Keiko tells the townspeople how the children discovered the stopped watch and how everyone helped restore it.
    Felix: A successful project, despite a minor communication difficulty.
    Andy: Minor for you, Felix.
    -> closing
+ [Invite Andy to explain the mystery.]
    Farmer: Andy, I think you should tell everyone how the mystery was solved.
    Andy: Me? Well, all right.
    Andy: Folks, I'm pleased to report that our missing watch was never stolen. It was simply receiving some overdue attention.
    Felix: Through properly authorized channels.
    Andy: And with enough paperwork to satisfy the entire county.
    -> closing
= closing
Keiko: Thank you both. I never meant to cause so much confusion.
Andy: You were trying to do something kind. Next time, we'll just make sure everyone knows what's happening.
Felix: I could prepare a standard notification form.
Andy: Let's not get carried away.
Farmer: At least the watch is working.
Andy: And everyone's happy. That's what matters.
Keiko: The children certainly are.
Andy: Well, that's one case closed. No culprit, no stolen property, and one very well-maintained pocket watch.
Felix: I'll make a note of it.
Andy: Of course you will.
-> END
=== complete ===
-> END
